WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.180
The Sea Witch lived at the edge of a dark place called Gooba.

2
00:00:08.181 --> 00:00:14.429
Its swirling waters were known to swallow up all kinds of creatures.

3
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.011
Most sea folk were afraid to swim near it.

4
00:00:18.012 --> 00:00:27.637
They’d heard scary stories about curious mermaids who swam too close to Gooba and never returned home.

5
00:00:27.638 --> 00:00:32.375
"Grandmother told me about the home of the Sea Witch when I was small,"

6
00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:36.094
the Little Mermaid thought as she swam along.

7
00:00:36.095 --> 00:00:39.473
"But it can’t be that awful."

8
00:00:39.474 --> 00:00:44.357
"Stop, Princess," a small fish suddenly cried out.

9
00:00:44.358 --> 00:00:48.055
"Do not go to that terrible place."

10
00:00:48.056 --> 00:00:52.258
"Don’t worry, little fish," said the Little Mermaid.

11
00:00:52.259 --> 00:00:57.094
Then she thought to herself, "The Sea Witch will grant my wish.

12
00:00:57.095 --> 00:01:00.091
I just know she will."

13
00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:06.979
The lovesick mermaid swam on and entered the gloomy realm of the Sea Witch.

14
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:13.606
"This place is as ugly as the Sea Kingdom is beautiful," she said to herself.

15
00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:19.946
Instead of gleaming, white sand, the sea floor here was dark and slimy.

16
00:01:19.947 --> 00:01:25.255
Mud seeped from every hole and every crack.

17
00:01:25.256 --> 00:01:29.542
"Where are the sea flowers?" wondered the Little Mermaid.

18
00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:34.682
"Where is the seaweed?"

19
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:42.109
"Get out of Gooba, Princess," hissed a snake from the mouth of a cave.

20
00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:45.470
"Who’s that?" asked the frightened mermaid.

21
00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:49.529
The snake vanished into the darkness of the cave.

22
00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:57.501
All of a sudden, the Little Mermaid saw twirling cones of water, twisting this way and that.

23
00:01:57.502 --> 00:02:01.860
The cones were swallowing up everything within reach.

24
00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:08.275
Anything that became caught in the churning water was sucked down into the mud.

25
00:02:08.276 --> 00:02:11.996
"I am not afraid," she said to herself.

26
00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:16.852
"My strong tail can take me around the danger easily."

27
00:02:16.853 --> 00:02:22.372
And she swam around each cone of whirling water in her path.

28
00:02:22.373 --> 00:02:29.285
Next she came to a muddy forest of thin trees with bony branches.

29
00:02:29.286 --> 00:02:36.246
Each long branch had twigs that moved like fingers, grabbing anything nearby.

30
00:02:36.247 --> 00:02:43.681
The trees’ sticky fingers held fish bones and pieces of wood from sunken ships.

31
00:02:43.682 --> 00:02:49.254
The skeletons of drowned sailors hung from the tree branches.

32
00:02:49.255 --> 00:02:55.067
"Oh dear," thought the Little Mermaid, "the trees never let go of their victims!"

33
00:02:55.068 --> 00:02:58.001
Terrified, she stopped.

34
00:02:58.002 --> 00:03:02.064
"I don’t think I can do this!" she cried.

35
00:03:02.065 --> 00:03:07.085
Her little heart thumped with fear and she almost turned back.

36
00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.397
But then she remembered her Prince.

37
00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:16.091
"For the sake of my love," she thought, "I must go on."

38
00:03:16.092 --> 00:03:22.607
Before she entered the forest, the mermaid braided her flowing hair close to her head.

39
00:03:22.608 --> 00:03:26.769
Then she darted through the water like a nimble fish.

40
00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:30.645
The slimy branches stretched out their fingers to seize her.

41
00:03:30.646 --> 00:03:33.563
But she was too fast.

42
00:03:33.564 --> 00:03:36.236
They could not catch her.

43
00:03:36.237 --> 00:03:40.637
Finally she reached a clearing in the sea forest.

44
00:03:40.638 --> 00:03:45.993
Fat worms stood guard and long snakes slithered about.

45
00:03:45.994 --> 00:03:50.436
The Little Mermaid saw a shack built of bones.

46
00:03:50.437 --> 00:03:55.578
The Sea Witch was sitting in front, picking her teeth with a seashell.

47
00:03:55.579 --> 00:04:01.120
With her tangled hair and beady eyes, she looked horrifying.

48
00:04:01.121 --> 00:04:06.417
At her feet sat a dozen pet frogs, croaking at her.

49
00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:08.607
"Welcome, Little Mermaid.

50
00:04:08.608 --> 00:04:13.332
I was expecting you," said the Sea Witch.

51
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:15.656
"And I know why you are here.

52
00:04:15.657 --> 00:04:18.559
You want to be a human.

53
00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.445
What a very foolish idea!"

54
00:04:21.446 --> 00:04:31.230
Then the Sea Witch began to laugh.

